  "turning_point_description": "May 7, 2025. India launches Operation Sindoor \u2014 strikes on 9 terror infrastructure targets in Pakistan and Pakistan-occupied Kashmir. 125 fighter jets from both sides are at standoff ranges. Targets include JeM (Markaz Subhan Allah, Bahawalpur \u2014 Masood Azhar's hometown compound), LeT (Makaz Raheel Shahid, Kotli), and Hizbul Mujahideen facilities. The strikes run 23-25 minutes. Rizwan Shah's ground-intelligence contribution enabled the precision target packages. The turning point: with strikes complete, Pakistan launches a blitz on Poonch (16 Indian civilians killed). Rizwan must assess Pakistani military intent \u2014 is this proportional retaliation heading to ceasefire, or the opening of a full conventional escalation toward nuclear threshold? The assessment determines whether to stay in Pakistan or exfiltrate.",
  "real_world_correlation": {
    "event_date": "May 7, 2025",
    "real_event": "India launched Operation Sindoor, striking 9 targets in Pakistan and PoK over 23-25 minutes. Targets included JeM's Markaz Subhan Allah (Bahawalpur), LeT's Makaz Raheel Shahid (Kotli PoK), and Hizbul Mujahideen camps. India claimed 70-100+ militants killed. Pakistan disputed civilian casualties. Pakistan retaliated with artillery strikes on Poonch, killing 16 Indian civilians. US Secretary of State Marco Rubio began ceasefire mediation immediately.",
    "first_india_pak_air_strikes_since_1971": "Operation Sindoor was the first Indian air strikes on Pakistani territory since the 1971 war. The political significance \u2014 crossing a half-century-old threshold \u2014 represents India's definitive abandonment of 'strategic restraint' as doctrine.",
    "precision_intelligence": "The precision of the strikes \u2014 9 specific terror infrastructure targets with reportedly no Pakistani military facilities hit (India's stated position) \u2014 required exceptional ground intelligence, signals intelligence, and satellite imagery over extended periods. RAW/DIA's intelligence preparation of the battlefield is reflected in the precision.",
    "munir_field_marshal_promotion": "General Asim Munir was promoted to Field Marshal on May 20, 2025 \u2014 two weeks after Operation Sindoor. The timing suggests the promotion was intended to bolster military morale and domestic narrative after India's strikes, not as a reward for military victory.",
    "tahawwur_rana_timing": "Tahawwur Rana arrived in India on April 10, 2025 \u2014 12 days before the Pahalgam attack and 27 days before Operation Sindoor. His extradition represents 26/11 accountability intersecting with the 2025 escalation cycle."
  },
